Description:
 linuxmuster-api7 - Api for the linuxmuster.net 7 server.
Changes:
 linuxmuster-api7 (1:7.4.16~edu) lmn74; urgency=medium
 .
   * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
     what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
   * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
     dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
     and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
     1:7.4.16~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.16 while still outranking
     every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all. The versioned
     dependencies on the fork's own packages therefore clamp on "(>=
     1:x.y.z~)", the Debian idiom that also accepts a tilde suffix.
   * Depend on linuxmuster-tools7 (>= 1:7.4.20~), so the fork cannot be mixed
     with the upstream package.
   * The github-release job asks for contents: write. The repository's
     default GITHUB_TOKEN permission is read, so creating the release would
     have failed with a 403 on the first tag. Granting it on the job keeps
     the default untouched for every other workflow.
   * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
     instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
